{"kind":"artifact","text":"Documentation candidate at exact head 33843691460da55c7c20fdca62db4e825bef0b86, covering the docs/ change the onboarding-identity core carries. This replaces the withdrawn candidate 76b50001, which stood at the defective 358a46d4.\n\nThe only page changed is docs/reference/architecture.md. It records the new host identity contract under layer 4: the fixed schema families, the witness declaration in force only when the initializing key signed it, delegation and revocation, resolution as the authority with no append gated, expiry judged against the sequencer's signed timestamp, and the package boundary and dependency-direction rows for host/identity. The compatibility table's surface axis now names the exported surface of host and host/identity.\n\nTwo corrections against the withdrawn candidate, both answering codex's findings.\n\nVouching. The earlier prose said self-signed is stronger than witnessed, describing a rung the code could not produce. The page now says one vouching rung is implemented — witnessed, where a deployment's key says a provider said so — and that the stronger rung, where the identity's own key signs, is deferred along with the providers that would occupy it, Nostr and a published forge signing key. It says why nothing names it: a value the code can never produce reads to a caller as a state to handle and to a reviewer as a rung that was built. The axis stays ordered so adding it later is one more value plus the reduction rule the verification axis already follows.\n\nThe bearer token. The provider-check paragraph now states the rule that keeps a person's token out of a log: no byte of provider- or transport-controlled text reaches an error from the check. A refusal is the numeric status with this program's own phrase for it; a transport failure or an unreadable answer is fixed words of the package's own. It records that substring redaction was considered and refused, because it removes only the spelling it goes looking for and the party echoing the credential chooses the spelling.\n\nThe page's rests_on frontmatter cites the live host artifact 969a4e7a alongside its existing bases, so it flares when the host contract moves under it.\n\nGATES, at this exact head: gofmt, build and vet clean; go test -count=1 ./... green including internal/docset, the uncached citation gate, which is what proves every citation on this page still resolves; go test -race -count=1 ./... green, exit 0.","body":{"commit":"33843691460da55c7c20fdca62db4e825bef0b86","path":"docs"}}